  "title": "FlexAttention backward compilation failure with GQA on NVIDIA B200",
  "issue_id": "160074",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nHey team,\n\nThe problem is as follows: triton fails to compile the FlexAttention backward when running with GQA on NVIDIA B200. Compiling MHA works with backends \"eager\", \"aot_eager\", \"inductor\", while GQA fails with backend \"inductor\" (the other two work).\n\nMinimal reproducer:\n```python\nimport torch\nfrom torch.nn.attention.flex_attention import flex_attention\n\ninductor = torch.compile(flex_attention, fullgraph=True, backend=\"inductor\")\n\nwith torch.device(\"cuda\"):\n    q = torch.randn([2, 32, 4096, 128], dtype=torch.bfloat16, requires_grad=True)\n    k = torch.randn([2, 8, 4096, 128], dtype=torch.bfloat16, requires_grad=True)\n    v = torch.randn([2, 8, 4096, 128], dtype=torch.bfloat16, requires_grad=True)\n\ny = inductor(q, k, v, enable_gqa=True)\ny.backward(torch.randn_like(y))\n```\n\nOn a side note, when switching to MHA, at least the forward attention call seems to be slower than expected. How well is B200 supported by FlexAttention?\n\nThanks!\n\n### Error logs\n\n```\nerror: Failures have been detected while processing an MLIR pass pipeline\nnote: Pipeline failed while executing [`TritonGPUHoistTMEMAlloc` on 'builtin.module' operation]\n...\nFile ~/x/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/backends/nvidia/compiler.py:298, in CUDABackend.make_ttgir(mod, metadata, opt, capability)\n    296 passes.common.add_sccp(pm)\n    297 passes.common.add_canonicalizer(pm)\n--> [298](https://file+.vscode-resource.vscode-cdn.net/Users/razvan/Downloads/~/x/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/backends/nvidia/compiler.py:298) pm.run(mod)\n    299 metadata[\"cluster_dims\"] = (cluster_info.clusterDimX, cluster_info.clusterDimY, cluster_info.clusterDimZ)\n    300 tensordesc_meta = mod.get_tensordesc_metadata()\n\nRuntimeError: PassManager::run failed\n```\n\n### Versions\n\nUnfortunately, I cannot run `collect_env.py` on the machine because I don't have access to it anymore, but this is coming from my custom system info dump that I've run at that time:\n```\nPlatform: Linux-6.1.144-170.251.amzn2023.x86_64-x86_64-with-glibc2.34\nPython Version: 3.10.12 (main, Jul 26 2023, 13:20:36) [Clang 16.0.3 ]\nPyTorch Version: 2.9.0.dev20250729+cu128\nTriton Version: 3.4.0\nDriver Version: 570.172.08\nCUDA Runtime Version (nvcc): 12.8\n```\n\ncc @chauhang @penguinwu @zou3519 @ydwu4 @bdhirsh @Chillee @drisspg @yanboliang @BoyuanFeng",
